{
  "id": "continuous-subarray-sum",
  "questionId": "continuous-subarray-sum",
  "slug": "continuous-subarray-sum",
  "title": "Continuous Subarray Sum",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Prefix sum",
  "patterns": [
    "prefix sum",
    "hash map"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "this is the same divisibility idea as counting subarrays divisible by k, but now you only need a yes/no answer, with a minimum length requirement - what changes?",
    "you only care about the EARLIEST index a remainder was seen, since that gives the longest possible gap for that remainder",
    "keep a hash map from remainder to the first index it occurred at (seed remainder 0 at index -1, to allow subarrays starting from index 0)",
    "if the current remainder has been seen before at index j, and the current index i satisfies i - j >= 2, you've found a valid subarray"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "not seeding remainder 0 at index -1, which misses valid subarrays starting at index 0",
    "overwriting a remainder's stored index every time it's seen again, instead of keeping only the first occurrence",
    "forgetting the length >= 2 requirement and accepting single-element matches"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array of integers, `nums`, and an integer `k`.\n\n**Determine whether `nums` has a contiguous subarray of length at least 2 whose sum is a multiple of `k`.**\n\nA sum of 0 counts as a multiple of every k.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= nums.length <= 20",
      "-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4",
      "1 <= k <= 200",
      "a qualifying subarray must have length at least 2"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "the only valid subarray is the entire array",
      "no subarray of length 2 or more is a multiple of k",
      "an array of length 1 (never valid, since length must be at least 2)"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
